Jinja fast-path probe pattern (from #469 FLA):   {% set has_col = false %}
  {% if execute %}
    {% set cols = adapter.get_columns_in_relation(ref('<table>')) %}
    {% set names = cols | map(attribute='name') | map('upper') | list %}
    {% set has_col = 'NEW_COL' in names %}
  {% endif %}
  {% if not has_col %}<slow-path CTE join on birth view, restricted to source-line keys>{% endif %}
Then in SELECT: {% if has_col %}t.new_col{% else %}slow_cte.new_col{% endif %}. Works both before and after the downstream table rebuilds — zero ops swap-over required.
